#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Synthwave now-playing screen and controller for the YouTube Music desktop app.

Talks to the app's API Server plugin (search, queue, like, shuffle, repeat,
live updates over a websocket), browses the YouTube Music library through
ytmusicapi, draws a cava visualizer and shows album art (kitty graphics
protocol, e.g. Ghostty). Falls back to playerctl (e.g. YouTube in Firefox)
when the app isn't reachable.

Now Playing is the master: it starts YouTube Music invisibly (the app's
appVisible/tray options are off) and quits it when the last window closes.

Keys: space play/pause, n next, p previous, l like, d dislike, s shuffle,
r repeat, / search, b library, tab queue, c cancel loading, q quit.
In lists: enter open/play, n play next, a add to queue, r radio, esc back.
Mouse: everything in the header is clickable (status, like/shuffle/repeat,
search/library/queue, artist, up next, prev/play/next), drag the time bar to
seek, click a row to select it and again to play it, wheel scrolls lists.
"""
